dem-long-list.gls -- dem-long-list.scm

The file: (define before-list 1), then (define big-list (quote ( ... )))
whose list has 100,000 lines of (item NNNNNN "ção € 😀" #\x 3.14 (nested
(deeper N))), then (define after-list 2).  6.8 MB, well closed.  In
the middle, lines 50003 to 50005 are a sublist indented wrong:

    (sublist 050000
(item 050001 ...)
                 (item 050002 ...))

Open:   chezweb dem-long-list.scm

1. C-n  C-M-f            from the start of line 2
   Expect: the cursor after ")))" at the end of big-list, within 2 s.
2. C-M-b                 Expect: back at the start of line 2, within 2 s.
3. M-g 50003 RET  C-M-f
                         Expect: the cursor after the (sublist ...), at
                         the end of line 50005, at once.
4. C-M-u                 Expect: the cursor on the ( that opens the list
                         of items (line 3), within 2 s.
5. C-M-SPC               mark-sexp (on the Mac, where C-M-SPC may change
                         the keyboard: M-x mark-sexp RET), then M-w
                         Expect: "Copied ..." (6.8 MB), within 2 s.
6. M->  C-y              Expect: 6.8 MB yanked at the end, within 2 s.
7. C-/                   Expect: the yank undone, within 2 s.
8. Indent the sublist:
   M-g 50003 RET         go to its first line, (sublist 050000;
   C-SPC                 set the mark there (C-@ if C-SPC changes the
                         keyboard);
   C-n C-n C-n           go down three lines;
   C-M-\                 indent the region (M-x indent-region).
                         Expect: the two (item ...) lines of the
                         sublist move to column 13, under 050000, and
                         "Indented 4 lines" (the region ends at the start
                         of a fourth line, which does not move).  It
                         takes about 11 seconds in the cloud, because the
                         editor reads the whole 6.8 MB list again for each
                         line.  Before 27 November it took six minutes,
                         and the editor seemed frozen.
9. C-x k RET, then "y": do not save.
